<p align="center">
  <b>Clean-room Windows x86-64 compatibility runtime for running Xbox Series (Scarlett) GDK / D3D12.X executables on PC Direct3D 12.</b><br>
  <a href="docs/design.md">Architecture</a> ·
  <a href="docs/building.md">Building &amp; Running</a> ·
  <a href="docs/legal.md">Scope &amp; Legal</a> ·
  <a href="tools/README.md">Components</a> ·
  <a href="CONTRIBUTING.md">Contributing</a>
</p>

VIKit maps an Xbox Series PE32+ executable natively on Windows x64, implements a clean-room host layer for Xbox/GDK APIs (`XMem`, `DirectStorage`, `AcpHal`, `GameInput`, `XAudio2`, `XTaskQueue`, `XAsync`), proxies `D3D12.X` and `PresentX` onto PC Direct3D 12, and provides RDNA2 (`gfx1013`) shader translation and Xbox texture detiling.

> [!NOTE]
> This repository contains **only original and GPL/MIT-licensed runtime source code and synthetic test fixtures**. It does not include any third-party software binaries, game files, copyrighted assets, keys, or DRM/entitlement bypasses.

---

## Architecture

| Component | Path | Purpose |
|---|---|---|
| **PE32+ Loader** | `tools/guest-loader` | Maps Xbox Series PE32+ binaries & companion DLLs natively on Windows x64 (relocations, TLS, `.pdata`, drive mapping, crash/JSONL tracing) |
| **GDK Host Layer** | `tools/gdk-host` | Clean-room implementations of `XMem` (write-watch GPU staging), `DirectStorage` (zlib + BCPack), `AcpHal`, `GameInput` (XInput + keyboard), `XAudio2`, `XTaskQueue`/`XAsync`, `dxcompiler_xs`, offline `XUser`/`XNetworking` stand-ins |
| **D3D12.X Proxy** | `tools/devicex-proxy` | COM wrapper over PC `ID3D12Device` with `+0x600` console inline-PM4 padding, `CreatePlacedResourceX`, `PresentX` bridge, shadow descriptor heaps (`xdesc`), CPU texture upload (`cpuup`), logical-HLSL binder, per-frame CSV frametimes, and window-bar CPU/RAM/VRAM/GPU telemetry |
| **PresentX Bridge** | `tools/presentx-bridge` | DXGI swapchain presentation and frame-pacing bridge |
| **Texture Detiling** | `tools/texture-boot`, `tools/detile` | Native GFX10/RDNA2 swizzle-pattern detiling (adapted from AMD AddrLib MIT) |
| **Shader Tooling** | `tools/shader-decode`, `tools/shader-translate` | RDNA2 (`gfx1013`) decoder (LLVM-verified) and HLSL/DXIL translation pipeline |
| **Runtime Trace** | `tools/runtime-trace` | Crash-safe JSONL event recorder shared by loader and proxy |

---

## Quick Start

### Requirements
- Windows 10 / 11 (x64) with a Direct3D 12 GPU
- MinGW-w64 UCRT (`gcc`, `g++`, `ar`) on `PATH`
- Python 3.10+
- Optional: Git Bash (for `.sh` helper scripts)

### 1. Build the Runtime

```powershell
powershell -ExecutionPolicy Bypass -File tools\guest-loader\build.ps1 -NoFixtures
```

This builds `tools\guest-loader\build\guest-loader.exe` and `tools\guest-loader\build\gdkhost_proxy.dll`.

### 2. Run an Executable

**PowerShell:**
```powershell
.\tools\guest-loader\run-title.ps1 -Exe "D:\Path\To\Package\title.exe"
```

**Git Bash:**
```bash
bash tools/guest-loader/run-title.sh /d/Path/To/Package/title.exe
```

Optional environment variables:
- `DEVICEX_DXIL_CACHE_MMAP` — path to a local pre-translated DXIL cache directory
- `DEVICEX_PRESENTX_MONITOR` — target display EDID vendor code (e.g. `DEL`, `SAM`, `MEI`)
- `DEVICEX_FRAMETIME_DUMP` — `1` (default) writes per-frame timing breakdown to `<run-dir>/frames/frametimes.csv`
- `GDKHOST_D3D12_DEBUG` — `1` enables the D3D12 debug layer

The live window title bar displays real-time FPS, frametime (ms), process CPU %, RAM usage, GPU VRAM usage/budget, and active GPU name for debugging.

### 3. Run Self-Checks (No External Binaries Required)

```powershell
python scripts\check_public_tree.py
python scripts\check_docs.py
```

